@startuml
title Tengine Lite - System Architecture Overview

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Examples" {
  [Vision/OCR Examples] as Examples
}

package "API Surfaces" {
  [C API] as CAPI
  [C++ API Docs] as CPPDocs
  [Python API Docs] as PYDocs
}

package "Tengine Lite Library" {
  [Scheduler] as Scheduler
  [Operator Module] as Operator
  [Device Backend] as Device
  [Serializer (tmfile)] as Serializer
}

package "Conversion Tooling" {
  [Linux Model Converter (CLI)] as LinuxConv
  [Online Model Converter (WebAssembly)] as WebConv
}

package "External Assets" {
  artifact "Image Files" as Img
  artifact "Model Files" as ModelFiles
  artifact "Binary tmfile" as TMFile
  artifact "Serialized Model Params" as SerParams
}

node "Linux" as LinuxNode
node "Web Browser (WASM)" as BrowserNode
node "Local Execution Environment" as LocalNode

component "CMake-based Build" as CMake

Examples --> CAPI : run examples
CAPI --> Scheduler
CPPDocs ..> CAPI : documentation entry point
PYDocs ..> CAPI : documentation entry point

Scheduler --> Operator : register/initialize operators
Scheduler --> Device : execute graphs on hardware
Scheduler --> Serializer : load/deserialize models
Serializer --> SerParams

Examples --> Img : consume local images

ModelFiles --> LinuxConv
ModelFiles --> WebConv
LinuxConv --> TMFile : produce
WebConv --> TMFile : produce
TMFile --> Serializer : decode

LinuxNode -- LinuxConv
BrowserNode -- WebConv
LocalNode -- Examples
LocalNode -- Scheduler

CMake ..> Scheduler : build
CMake ..> Examples : build

note left of Examples
Includes: classification, detection, segmentation,
pose estimation, landmarks, OCR
end note

note bottom of CAPI
Compatible with original Tengine C API
end note

note right of WebConv
Executes locally via WebAssembly
No external network required
end note

note bottom of CMake
Cross-platform build based on CMake
end note

@enduml
